      "why": "Pipelined_m registers every m stages, reducing FF count compared to fully pipelined while maintaining 1-result/cycle throughput. This is a direct area trade-off: fewer pipeline registers = fewer FFs, but potentially lower Fmax due to longer combinational paths. For m=2..4, the latency is ceil(N/m)+2 cycles. With N=12..18 and m=2..4, latency ranges from ~5 to 11 cycles, well within the 0.44us budget. The accuracy is identical to pipelined for the same data_width/n_iter/guards/rounding, so the trade-off is purely area (LUTs+FFs) vs Fmax. This family likely produces designs with fewer FFs than pipelined, potentially dominating on the luts_plus_ffs objective if Fmax remains adequate. m=2..4 balances FF savings against timing closure risk."
